<p>Command line <code>&gt; perl cross.pl in=250k_dict.txt ws=-1 rx=[st] dist=1 quiet</code><br />
But you can use this <code>&gt; perl cross.pl in=250k_dict.txt ws=-1 quiet</code> and<br />
send it on its way.<br />
Or use <code>&gt; perl cross.pl in=250k_dict.txt ws=-1 dist=2</code> to just get letter distribution, then exit (see usage text ).</p>
<p>This dictionary sample took less than 3 hours to generate<br />
all 21 Intermediate files for it.<br />
Only need to be generated once per Dictionary.</p>
<p>This is the log file of the generation results <a href="https://regexformat.com/dnl/_Samples/_Cross_Misc/_00Ltr_HDR.txt" rel="nofollow noreferrer">_00Ltr_HDR.txt</a></p>
<p>Command line usage <em><a href="https://regexformat.com/dnl/_Samples/_Cross_Misc/Cross.pl" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Cross . pl</a></em> :</p>
<pre><code>Usage:  Cross.pl  -  Intermediate file generator

   Reqd:  &lt;In=word-file-name-in.txt&gt;  input name of dictionary (single word/line)
          &lt;ws=3-#&gt;  word size ranges (3 letters minimum)
          &lt;ws=-1&gt;   or  -1 will do all sizes

   Opt:   &lt;Out=file-name-out-root&gt;  prepended to '#Ltr.txt' output name
          &lt;rx=[st]&gt; filter regex, calls Cross_Qry.pl
          &lt;dist=1&gt;  1 or 2 ? print letter distribution.  2 ? then exits
          &lt;quiet&gt;   suppress word list display of generated difs
</code></pre>
<p>Command line usage <em><a href="https://regexformat.com/dnl/_Samples/_Cross_Misc/Cross_Qry.pl" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Cross_Qry . pl</a></em></p>
<pre><code>Usage: Cross_Qry.pl

  Reqd:  &lt;In=Intermediate-file-name.txt&gt;
         &lt;rx=[st]&gt;  regex filter
  Opt:   &lt;Out=file-capture-root&gt;  prepended to '_Filt.txt' output name
         &lt;quiet&gt;   supress word list display of generated difs
</code></pre>
